        "original_id": "c5d5795e-23ad-5cf9-9344-e14a1e014af1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Babcock State Park, New River Gorge, Fayette County, West Virginia, New River Gorge Bridge, Hinton, Hawks Nest State Park, Ansted\n- Organizations: United States National Park Service\n- Protected Areas: New River Gorge National River\n\nFacts:\n- Babcock State Park is a state park on 4,127 wooded acres in Fayette County, West Virginia, along the New River Gorge.\n- Babcock State Park is located about 20 miles from the New River Gorge Bridge.\n- In 1978, the United States National Park Service established New River Gorge National River to protect and maintain the New River Gorge in southern West Virginia.\n- New River Gorge National River extends 53 miles from just downstream of Hinton to Hawks Nest State Park near Ansted.",
